subproblems.statement:
Let N, n ∈ ℕ and write H^n := μHE[n], the n-dimensional Euclidean Hausdorff measure on ℝ^N = Euclidean N. Let μ be a measure on ℝ^N (Borel σ-algebra). Let M, K ⊆ ℝ^N, with M H^n-null-measurable and K Borel, and let θ, h : ℝ^N → ℝ. Assume:
- θ(y) > 0 for every y ∈ M;
- θ is H^n-integrable on M ∩ K;
- μ(B) = ∫⁻_{B ∩ M} ENNReal.ofReal(θ(y)) dH^n(y) for every Borel set B ⊆ ℝ^N;
- h(z) = 0 for every z ∉ K.
Then the Bochner integrals satisfy ∫ h dμ = ∫_M h(z) θ(z) dH^n(z). No measurability, boundedness or integrability of h is assumed; a Bochner integral of a non-integrable function is 0.
